  "caveats": {
    "scope": "Names the fold state of a step that succeeded. It does not detect an incomplete fold: on failed fold frames it spreads its answers over the classes at high confidence (see sanity_checks.failed_fold_checks). Use the check verdict head (#91) to decide whether a fold succeeded.",
    "triangle_fold": "Unsupported. No frame in the data shows a triangle fold, so the head can only answer empty, flat, half or quarter. Human fold labels from the labelling workstream (#87) are the path to add it, but its visual taxonomy (crepe-visual-v2) has no triangle label yet; the follow-up (#106) depends on adding one.",
    "label_leakage": "Weak labels: the class equals the check that took the frame. The head may learn check-specific camera timing or plate state instead of the fold shape. sanity_checks.geometry tests this with failed folds that changed nothing (small n, stated there). Still-flat crepes after a failed fold1 are named flat (pass). Still-half crepes after a failed fold2 are never named half (fail): by eye they are half folds turned sideways, which no training frame shows, and the head reads the wedge as quarter or the pan as empty. The likely cause is rotation: the head reads the wedge's orientation, not the fold, so half vs quarter is only shown to work in the robot's normal fold pose. Follow-up: rotation augmentation (#103) and rotation robustness plus the check against human labels on video frames (#104).",
    "empty": "empty is learned from passed plate_clean frames only and tested on passed plate_present frames, a check it never trained on.",
